  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Capacity of Africa Faith Actors Network for Climate Justice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project seeks to build on the achievements made by the AFAN-CJ from the previous interventions through local, national, regional and global advocacy and community-led initiatives that promote climate justice. This will also promote the growth of the network in membership and increase its visibility in new countries where AACC&#x2019;s member churches are present. This is in recognition that some countries are not well represented in the membership of the network, especially persons from other religious faiths. This reality militates against broad participation, visibility, and vibrancy in the entire continent. Therefore, the AACC will continue to facilitate and encourage the recruitment of new AFAN-CJ members in countries that are not or least represented in the network and also strengthen their capacity for climate change processes and issues in this new phase of cooperation. The AACC shall endeavor to maintain balanced participation of the youth, women, PWDs, and other faiths beyond Christians and Muslims in the AFAN-CJ.</narrative>
  </description>
